From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 31 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fix simultaneous losses, FFA draw end and battle
 defaults

Four fixes for more than two duelists.

Several duelists can lose in one check. Before, each loser was marked
and run one after the other. A later body saw an earlier loser as alive,
so it sent cards to a dead seat (index 255 in SendTo under UBSan). Now
check_losses_n marks every loser dead first, then runs each body.
field::eliminate has a "marked" flag for a duelist that is already
flagged. Each loser gets exactly one message 200.

A free for all that ends in a draw wrote only MSG_WIN. Now it writes one
200 per loser (same reason as a normal loss) before MSG_WIN. A Tag end
is unchanged: MSG_WIN only.

BattleCommand started with reason_player PLAYER_NONE, which is seat 2
at n > 2. The unit header cannot call none_id(), so the constructor now
takes the value and all 4 creation sites in processor.cpp pass
none_id().

A direct attack with no valid pick now skips the damage at n > 2 in
calculate_battle_damage. The old pd != pa guard already did this, so
the skip is explicit and no damage message is written.

A two-duelist duel is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
